 {
  "id": "opDemoLeadIntake1",
  "name": "op: DEMO \u2014 Lead intake with retries + dead-letter",
  "nodes": [
   {
    "id": "5794be06-052f-4d87-a8d6-34c1cfc76240",
    "name": "About this demo",
    "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
    "typeVersion": 1,
    "position": [
     -80,
     -260
    ],
    "parameters": {
     "content": "## op: DEMO \u2014 Lead intake with retries + dead-letter\nReference build by Occelatus Labs to show our error-handling pattern (not a client workflow).\n1. Validate input \u2192 400 on bad payloads\n2. Idempotency key \u2192 duplicates are a no-op\n3. CRM push retries 3\u00d7 (2s apart)\n4. Still failing \u2192 dead-letter queue + on-call alert (mock), caller gets 202\n5. Anything unexpected \u2192 workflow-level Error Workflow\nSend `simulate_failure: true` to force the failure path.",
     "height": 300,
     "width": 420
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "9ca20555-ae7e-4f5c-b1c0-fd1e7ff64cec",
    "name": "Receive lead (webhook)",
    "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
    "typeVersion": 2,
    "position": [
     0,
     100
    ],
    "parameters": {
     "httpMethod": "POST",
     "path": "op-demo-lead",
     "responseMode": "responseNode",
     "options": {}
    },
    "webhookId": "d938bb66-b13f-438a-8db2-2e03de95fdb1"
   },
   {
    "id": "00f59228-eb4d-4dcf-80b4-e65b2270d817",
    "name": "Validate + build idempotency key",
    "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
    "typeVersion": 2,
    "position": [
     220,
     100
    ],
    "parameters": {
     "jsCode": "// Validate the payload and build an idempotency key (same lead twice = same key).\nconst out = [];\nfor (const item of $input.all()) {\n  const b = item.json.body || item.json;\n  const email = String(b.email || '').trim().toLowerCase();\n  const name = String(b.name || '').trim();\n  const errors = [];\n  if (!/^[^@\\s]+@[^@\\s]+\\.[^@\\s]+$/.test(email)) errors.push('email missing or invalid');\n  if (!name) errors.push('name missing');\n  out.push({ json: {\n    valid: errors.length === 0, errors,\n    lead: { name, email, message: String(b.message || '').slice(0, 2000) },\n    idempotencyKey: email + '|' + String(b.submitted_at || b.message || '').slice(0, 64),\n    simulateFailure: b.simulate_failure === true,\n  }});\n}\nreturn out;"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "2023628c-a8bc-477d-8420-c3073a229975",
    "name": "Payload valid?",
    "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
    "typeVersion": 2,
    "position": [
     440,
     100
    ],
    "parameters": {
     "conditions": {
      "options": {
       "caseSensitive": true,
       "leftValue": "",
       "typeValidation": "strict"
      },
      "conditions": [
       {
        "id": "3e340094-fe94-4552-8d1b-d36bdb98fb4e",
        "leftValue": "={{ $json.valid }}",
        "rightValue": true,
        "operator": {
         "type": "boolean",
         "operation": "true",
         "singleValue": true
        }
       }
      ],
      "combinator": "and"
     },
     "options": {}
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "c682c3be-1ae3-4fe9-836e-0b1fb3c263ca",
    "name": "Respond 400 \u2014 invalid payload",
    "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
    "typeVersion": 1.1,
    "position": [
     660,
     280
    ],
    "parameters": {
     "respondWith": "json",
     "responseBody": "={{ { ok: false, errors: $json.errors } }}",
     "options": {
      "responseCode": 400
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "45e24b33-d0cc-43e4-ae04-1c3fcd043f25",
    "name": "Skip already-processed leads",
    "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
    "typeVersion": 2,
    "position": [
     660,
     0
    ],
    "parameters": {
     "jsCode": "// Skip leads we've already pushed (survives retries and double-submits).\nconst seen = $getWorkflowStaticData('global');\nseen.keys = seen.keys || {};\nreturn $input.all().map(i => ({ json: { ...i.json, duplicate: Boolean(seen.keys[i.json.idempotencyKey]) } }));"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "de28364f-c399-4010-9538-dbae8f3f0269",
    "name": "Already processed?",
    "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
    "typeVersion": 2,
    "position": [
     880,
     0
    ],
    "parameters": {
     "conditions": {
      "options": {
       "caseSensitive": true,
       "leftValue": "",
       "typeValidation": "strict"
      },
      "conditions": [
       {
        "id": "a8dafdb7-eb9f-4ce4-a21c-103c50708d0e",
        "leftValue": "={{ $json.duplicate }}",
        "rightValue": true,
        "operator": {
         "type": "boolean",
         "operation": "true",
         "singleValue": true
        }
       }
      ],
      "combinator": "and"
     },
     "options": {}
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "45824260-8ab8-4dbd-bc08-43d3a67893d4",
    "name": "Respond 200 \u2014 duplicate, no-op",
    "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
    "typeVersion": 1.1,
    "position": [
     1100,
     -160
    ],
    "parameters": {
     "respondWith": "json",
     "responseBody": "={{ { ok: true, duplicate: true } }}",
     "options": {
      "responseCode": 200
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "5caba195-bdb9-451c-a7db-ffa29e06878a",
    "name": "Push lead to CRM (mock)",
    "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
    "typeVersion": 4.2,
    "position": [
     1100,
     60
    ],
    "parameters": {
     "method": "POST",
     "url": "={{ $json.simulateFailure ? 'https://httpbin.org/status/503' : 'https://httpbin.org/post' }}",
     "sendBody": true,
     "specifyBody": "json",
     "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json.lead) }}",
     "options": {
      "timeout": 10000
     }
    },
    "retryOnFail": true,
    "maxTries": 3,
    "waitBetweenTries": 2000,
    "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
   },
   {
    "id": "5fdcae7e-3400-4001-9a7c-73d41e60e792",
    "name": "Mark lead processed",
    "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
    "typeVersion": 2,
    "position": [
     1340,
     -40
    ],
    "parameters": {
     "jsCode": "// Record the key only AFTER the CRM accepted it, so a failed push can be retried later.\nconst seen = $getWorkflowStaticData('global');\nseen.keys = seen.keys || {};\nconst lead = $('Skip already-processed leads').first().json;\nseen.keys[lead.idempotencyKey] = new Date().toISOString();\nreturn [{ json: { status: 'accepted', key: lead.idempotencyKey } }];"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "264613cd-8f8d-4cac-8d79-94937728bb03",
    "name": "Respond 200 \u2014 accepted",
    "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
    "typeVersion": 1.1,
    "position": [
     1560,
     -40
    ],
    "parameters": {
     "respondWith": "json",
     "responseBody": "={{ { ok: true, status: 'accepted' } }}",
     "options": {
      "responseCode": 200
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "a7e23094-408a-4c6c-bb94-e5710241bd72",
    "name": "Build dead-letter record",
    "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
    "typeVersion": 2,
    "position": [
     1340,
     180
    ],
    "parameters": {
     "jsCode": "// Build a dead-letter record: what failed, why, and the full lead so nothing is lost.\nconst lead = $('Skip already-processed leads').first().json;\nconst err = $json.error || {};\nreturn [{ json: {\n  failed_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n  step: 'Push lead to CRM (mock)',\n  attempts: 3,\n  error: err.message || JSON.stringify(err).slice(0, 300),\n  lead: lead.lead, idempotencyKey: lead.idempotencyKey,\n}}];"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "6bc92470-7195-4e8a-81bf-853ad47ae041",
    "name": "Save to dead-letter queue",
    "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
    "typeVersion": 2,
    "position": [
     1560,
     180
    ],
    "parameters": {
     "jsCode": "// Keep the failed lead in a dead-letter queue (workflow static data) so it can be replayed by hand.\nconst store = $getWorkflowStaticData('global');\nstore.deadLetter = store.deadLetter || [];\nstore.deadLetter.push($json);\nreturn [{ json: { ...$json, queued: store.deadLetter.length } }];"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "c80616dd-bb80-4b3d-9b01-2e9fd3431d53",
    "name": "Notify on-call (mock webhook)",
    "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
    "typeVersion": 4.2,
    "position": [
     1780,
     180
    ],
    "parameters": {
     "method": "POST",
     "url": "https://httpbin.org/post",
     "sendBody": true,
     "specifyBody": "json",
     "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ alert: 'Lead push failed after 3 tries', email: $json.lead.email, error: $json.error, queued: $json.queued }) }}",
     "options": {
      "timeout": 10000
     }
    },
    "retryOnFail": true,
    "maxTries": 2,
    "waitBetweenTries": 1000
   },
   {
    "id": "8b7b3df9-fcd1-4b70-823e-1e55891e35b4",
    "name": "Respond 202 \u2014 queued for follow-up",
    "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
    "typeVersion": 1.1,
    "position": [
     2000,
     180
    ],
    "parameters": {
     "respondWith": "json",
     "responseBody": "={{ { ok: true, status: 'queued_for_manual_follow_up' } }}",
     "options": {
      "responseCode": 202
     }
    }
   }
  ],
